    "q-118069": {
      "dom_id": "step-q118069",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "The sum of the interior angles of a polygon is ${3960}^{∘}.$ How many sides does it have?",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the sum of the interior angles of a polygon with $n$ sides is ${180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2).$\n\nTo find the number of sides in our polygon, we start by setting up the following equation:\n\n$$\n{180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2)=3\\,{960}^{∘}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $n,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2) & =3\\,{960}^{∘} \\\\ n-2 & =\\frac{3\\,{960}^{∘}}{{180}^{∘}} \\\\ n-2 & =22 \\\\ n & =24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the polygon has $n=24$ sides.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
